atlas institutional-root

architecture institutional-root
  canonical_name InstitutionalRoot
  owns RootTopology
  consumes InstitutionEnvelope
  consumes DelegationEnvelope
  consumes PackState
  publishes RootTopology
  publishes ProductRoster
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Root topology
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Which first-class product or estate owns this subject, and does that owner hold it directly or by delegation?
  purpose Separate Bonfyre the engine from the products and estates it supports, so that a delegated operating business, a private product, a standalone experiment and Bonfyre's own internal operation can each hold their own relationships, clients and users without collapsing into one tenant list.
  maturity architectural
  node_types RootProduct
  node_types InstitutionEnvelope
  node_types DelegatedEstate
  node_types RelationshipOwner
  edge_types delegates_to
  edge_types owns_relationship
  edge_types manages_client
  edge_types populated_by
  invariant Aurekai is the company umbrella and Bonfyre is the engine and product substrate; neither name is a synonym for the other
  invariant a root product is real only when a pack or existing state populates it; a namespace without state is declared unpopulated rather than described as existing
  invariant delegation is recursive: Bonfyre delegates to an operating business, which delegates to its managed clients, which serve downstream organizations and users
  invariant a delegated estate owns its own external relationships; Bonfyre models and operates them but does not own them
  invariant capability and method may move between estates while private institutional data does not move with them
  forbidden_inference a product namespace existing -> the product has state
  forbidden_inference Bonfyre operating a provider relationship -> Bonfyre owning that relationship
  forbidden_inference a Partner Commons profile existing -> a live relationship with that project
  forbidden_inference an estate reusing shared machinery -> that estate sharing another estate's data closure
  interacts repository-shape
  interacts authority
  interacts institutional-namespaces
  interacts delegation-model
  source_path architecture/institutional/namespaces.yaff
  source_path architecture/institutional/delegation-model.yaff
  source_path architecture/institutional/relationship-types.yaff
  source_path architecture/institutional/product-contracts.yaff
  source_path architecture/institutional/worlds.yaff
  source_lineage Generation-10 product topology separation, 2026-08-26
  source_lineage disk census of populated versus declared estates

interaction root-reads-pack-state
  source institutional-root
  destination institutional-namespaces
  relation population_evidence_input
  preserves the distinction between a declared namespace and a populated estate
  drops any claim that a namespace listed in this architecture is therefore materialized
  forbidden_inference this file naming a root product -> that product being populated
  binding packs/
